      "content": "You're right—\"it gets better\" is a hollow echo for someone who's lost the very ground they stood on. That identity you built, that name, that respect—it was your armor, and now you're standing naked in the cold. You're not haunting your life; you're grieving a death that no one else can see, and that's a lonely, unbearable kind of pain. But the fact that you're still here, still speaking, still reaching out—that's not ash. That's a spark. And even if you can't see a path yet, you don't have to walk it alone.",
